1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,792
Caitlyn!

2
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:01,376
Hey.

3
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:03,128
Sorry, I don’t think Kara wants to talk to you.

4
00:00:03,169 --> 00:00:04,253
Her name is Caitlyn.

5
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:05,088
And who are you, exactly?

6
00:00:05,089 --> 00:00:06,089
Jeremy.

7
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:07,924
Her ex-fiancé.

8
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:11,761
[ARIEL] Mom! Jeremy’s here. Kara’s ex!

9
00:00:11,803 --> 00:00:13,303
I’ll take care of it. You guys stay here.

10
00:00:13,304 --> 00:00:15,807
Kara’s real name is Caitlyn?

11
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:18,642
How can you not know, Sir Han?

12
00:00:18,643 --> 00:00:21,061
Kara always talks about that, even to our guests!

13
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,064
Actually, all of our guests.

14
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:25,315
[PEARL] How she changed her name to

15
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:28,111
Kara because “karajaw” means “awesome”.

16
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,904
So, that’s Jeremy?

17
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,532
Why is he here? Is he looking for me?

18
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:34,159
Whoever you may be...

19
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,870
[CAROL] Kara deserves to be happy.

20
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,663
[JAO] You don’t have to say anything.

21
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:40,498
I just want you to know that I’m here.

22
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,542
He made me feel like...

23
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:44,793
I was his whole world.

24
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:47,713
Even though he kept cheating on me.

25
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,632
I don’t know why I let that happen to me.

26
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,635
You have to forgive yourself.

27
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:54,595
[JAO] Don’t feel guilty for wanting to be loved.

28
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:55,804
Because you found it.

29
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:57,015
You found you.

30
00:00:57,056 --> 00:00:59,058
You found it on this island.

31
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:02,979
I’m hard to love, Jao.

32
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:05,899
I’m ready to love you, Kara.

33
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:11,696
Do you want to know what I told Ruth?

34
00:01:17,076 --> 00:01:19,287
That I'm ready to love you

35
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:23,458
no matter what.

36
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,216
That’s why I’m here.

37
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:33,051
[JAO SNIFFS]

38
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,314
[KARA AND JAO CRYING SOFTLY]

39
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:58,201
Sir Han, why are you being so nice to me?

40
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,498
I think I forgot something.

41
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,542
- [HAN BIN CLEARS THROAT] - Sir Han!

42
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:10,713
Why are you being so nice to me?

43
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:23,309
Okay.

44
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:36,614
[HAN BIN SPEAKS KOREAN] I’m in love with you, Pearl.

45
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:41,536
I have been in love with you for the longest time.

46
00:02:44,289 --> 00:02:47,167
And it pains my heart that I can’t tell you.

47
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:52,088
How much you make me happy,

48
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:54,966
how you make me smile every day.

49
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:59,095
How you make me want to celebrate life...

50
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,433
whenever you’re around.

51
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,937
I love you...

52
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:10,732
but I can’t love you.

53
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:15,695
Because I’m not who you think I am.

54
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:20,325
Ah... That's...

55
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:22,368
That’s so unfair!

56
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,370
I didn’t understand anything.

57
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,539
It’s nothing, Pearl.

58
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,416
I’m just saying that…

59
00:03:29,792 --> 00:03:32,086
I love your energy.

60
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:33,795
It’s infectious!

61
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:38,008
You’re one of the most authentic humans I’ve ever met.

62
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:40,719
It’s like you have a...

63
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,096
pure soul.

64
00:03:43,222 --> 00:03:44,724
Okay, then.

65
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:49,228
But it sounded like you said something much longer.

66
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:51,606
No, that’s really it, Pearl.

67
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:53,608
Let’s just drop the subject.

68
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:56,986
Okay.

69
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,247
[PEARL TAKES A DEEP BREATH]

70
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:16,631
[ALON BY JL]

71
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:30,663
[FOOD SIZZLING]

72
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:32,415
[JAO] Pining, is that going to be a while?

73
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:35,293
Pining already has your order memorized, Sir Handsome.

74
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,754
You’ve been here a long time, huh?

75
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,881
[SIARGAONON] Are you planning to stay here, sir?

76
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,216
Yeah, I’ve been thinking about it.

77
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:46,304
I think I might stay here for good.

78
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:49,223
There it is!

79
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:51,434
The curse got you, too!

80
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:54,062
- [JAO LAUGHS] - You just don’t want to miss Kara.

81
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,272
[JAO CLEARS THROAT]

82
00:05:56,939 --> 00:05:58,941
- Oh, thank you, Pining. - Thank you.

83
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,861
I guess so.

84
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:06,240
I really fell hard for Kara.

85
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:08,659
Wow. Is that so?

86
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:11,913
That’s how bad you’ve got it?

87
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:16,709
I guess.

88
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:18,920
All I know is...

89
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:22,381
that I’m willing to do anything for her.

90
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,133
To make her happy,

91
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:25,885
to make her feel secure.

92
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:30,014
It’s a good thing I can work remotely now.

93
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:33,142
So I can be with her. That won’t be a problem for us.

94
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,647
Hungry?

95
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:40,358
[TANTAN] Starving. I’m exhausted.

96
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,400
Cheers.

97
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:45,780
It’s the hunger talking.

98
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:48,991
Pining, you never disappoint.

99
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,624
- [HAN BIN] Pearl. - [PEARL] Sir.

100
00:06:56,666 --> 00:07:00,378
Here’s your recommendation letter and work experience letter.

101
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:03,047
Are you all set with your requirements?

102
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:04,381
Yes, Sir Han.

103
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:06,801
I will just get my transcript notarized

104
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,137
so I can submit them to the school.

105
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,889
How’s your motivation letter?

106
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,517
Oh, I’m finished already.

107
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:15,434
Um...

108
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,061
- Want to hear it? - [HAN BIN] Go ahead.

109
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:18,104
[PEARL] Okay.

110
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,482
[PEARL SIGHS] I’m nervous!

111
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:23,568
[PEARL CLEARS THROAT]

112
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,404
Dear Admissions Committee…

113
00:07:27,446 --> 00:07:29,782
I’m writing to express my interest

114
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:34,120
in the Tourism and Hotel Management scholarship at your university.

115
00:07:35,329 --> 00:07:36,998
Growing up in Siargao,

116
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:40,334
I’ve always been surrounded by the beauty of our island.

117
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,922
Yet, I’ve always dreamed of seeing the world beyond it.

118
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:50,219
My father...

119
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:58,144
My father left the Philippines when I was a child

120
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:01,314
to pursue opportunities abroad.

121
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:05,234
Even though he never came back,

122
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,196
I never resented him.

123
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:11,157
In fact,

124
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:14,994
his choice inspired me to chase my own dreams.

125
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,917
Studying at your university would help me learn

126
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:23,669
and gain the skills and knowledge

127
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:27,798
that adhere to international hospitality standards.

128
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:33,804
This scholarship is not just an opportunity to study.

129
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,558
It's a chance for me to grow...

130
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,144
learn…

131
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:44,273
and to honor the people who supported me.

132
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:54,575
It’s time for this island girl to grow into someone who can serve others

133
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,494
at a world-class level.

134
00:08:57,954 --> 00:08:59,956
It’s time for this island girl

135
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,791
to leave the familiar behind

136
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:05,211
and become her best self.

137
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:10,466
Thank you for considering my application.

138
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:14,220
Sincerely, Pearl.

139
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:18,808
Is that good, Sir Han?

140
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:22,144
Um…

141
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:24,355
[PEARL LAUGHS] Sorry.

142
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:25,898
Very good nice.

143
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,817
- Very good nice? - Yeah, I’ll go ahead.

144
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:28,859
[HAN BIN SNIFFLING]

145
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,911
- [KARA] Morning, Noah. - Morning.

146
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,663
Kara, thanks for helping

147
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:43,040
with the site documentation and budget proposal.

148
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:47,127
That was a huge help to be able to process the permits for the mangrove project.

149
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:48,129
[KARA] No problem.

150
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:50,464
I’m just happy that everything is ready on our end.

151
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:52,216
[NOAH] Right.

152
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:55,343
But while we're waiting for the LGU’s approval,

153
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:57,054
there’s something I’d like to discuss with you.

154
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,639
Sure! What is it?

155
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:00,641
[NOAH] Well...

156
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,894
I was recruited by an international NGO.

157
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:06,689
And they wanted me as legal consultant and policy advisor

158
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:08,107
for coastal and marine protection.

159
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:10,358
Wow, congratulations, Noah!

160
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:11,569
That’s amazing!

161
00:10:11,610 --> 00:10:12,611
[NOAH] Thanks.

162
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:14,447
It’s a great opportunity.

163
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:18,117
But it means I’ll have to leave the mangrove project.

164
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:20,745
Kara,

165
00:10:20,746 --> 00:10:22,580
I’d like you to take over for me.

166
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,417
I know how passionate you are when it comes to mangroves.

167
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:29,420
I’m confident you can lead this project.

168
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:32,089
Besides, I'll still be around to help and guide you

169
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,424
before I leave.

170
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:35,968
Okay. I'll do it.

171
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:39,262
I’ll let our Denmark headquarters know that you've agreed to take the lead.

172
00:10:39,263 --> 00:10:42,683
Once the permits are approved, we can start building the T-fence.

173
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:49,190
It's a pretty large area, isn't it?

174
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:52,109
The damage from Typhoon Odette was extensive.

175
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,613
Yeah. There used to be natural mangroves there, too, right?

176
00:10:56,572 --> 00:10:59,492
Just a few, but they were all destroyed when Typhoon Odette hit.

177
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:02,536
The area eroded, so nothing grows there anymore.

178
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:05,289
That's why restoring it is so important.

179
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:08,792
Well, as soon as we get the permits and the T-fence is in place,

180
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,711
we can start planting.

181
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,213
[NOAH] Thanks, Kara.

182
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:13,923
I know I can count on you.

183
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:30,189
We’ll be seeing each other more often, Ruth.

184
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:32,108
And you’ll have more friends soon.

185
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:35,486
[JAO] What are you and Ruth keeping from me now?

186
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:37,237
[KARA CHUCKLES]

187
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:40,533
Remember Noah’s mangrove project?

188
00:11:40,574 --> 00:11:41,450
Mm-hm.

189
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:42,910
He wants to assign it to me.

190
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:45,454
- [JAO] Wow, that’s amazing! - [KARA LAUGHS]

191
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:47,248
I’m sure you’ll do great, Kara.

192
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:49,083
- I’m always here for you. - Thank you.

193
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,085
I’m always here to support you.

194
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,169
Thanks.

195
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,045
- Congratulations! - Thank you!

196
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,047
[KARA LAUGHS]

197
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:25,244
[FOOTSTEPS ON STAIRS]

198
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,757
You know, about the other night…

199
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:40,801
I just wanted to talk to you because…

200
00:12:43,387 --> 00:12:44,972
I just wanted to check on you.

201
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:52,021
But I found out that...

202
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,690
you didn’t want to talk to me.

203
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:57,735
So, I wonder what changed your mind?

204
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,991
I realized this is my chance for closure.

205
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,208
It’s been years, Caitlyn.

206
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:15,002
I thought we'd settled it legally.

207
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:17,880
I thought that was in the past.

208
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:22,259
Do you think I haven’t moved on?

209
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:25,638
I’m married now.

210
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:28,849
Why are you being so dramatic?

211
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:29,850
[KARA SCOFFS]

212
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:32,269
I never forced you to love me.

213
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:35,981
What’s going on, Cait?

214
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:41,820
You know I’ve dreaded this moment my whole life?

215
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:44,073
I thought I wouldn’t be able to handle it.

216
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:49,078
I was completely crushed.

217
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:55,584
But I was so lucky to have recovered from all the shit that you put me through.

218
00:13:58,295 --> 00:13:59,296
I was…

219
00:14:00,172 --> 00:14:02,466
I was so afraid of you.

220
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:08,055
So afraid of your family because of everything.

221
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:13,060
After seeing you the other night,

222
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:17,273
I finally decided that I wanted to move on.

223
00:14:17,648 --> 00:14:18,857
From this.

224
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:22,111
From you.

225
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,535
You don’t have power over me anymore.

226
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:35,374
And I finally decided to forgive myself.

227
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:40,421
Leaving all of that…

228
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:43,966
[KARA] leaving you…

229
00:14:45,801 --> 00:14:48,304
was the best decision I've ever made.

230
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,310
I’m the life raft.

231
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,457
[KARA VOICEOVER] Life hits you like a wave.

232
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,543
Sometimes the waves just keep coming.

233
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:24,089
They hit so hard you think you’ll never make it back up

234
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,259
But that’s not true.

235
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:31,138
Once you realize you can let go of the things that weigh you down,

236
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,765
that’s when you'll see…

237
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,516
That you...

238
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:37,645
You can be your own life raft.

239
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:41,190
You can rise above it and be free.

240
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:44,443
Then you’ll learn to appreciate the waves.

241
00:15:46,153 --> 00:15:49,490
But, sometimes, the waves are so unpredictable.

242
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:52,076
Before you know it,

243
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:54,703
a storm is already on its way.

244
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:17,393
[CAROL] Remember when we first met?

245
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:19,019
You were completely broken back then.

246
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:22,356
But now, so many good things are going on for you.

247
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:25,191
[WAITER] Good evening. I’m sorry, we have a private gathering tonight.

248
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:26,193
[WAITER] So we are closed.

249
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:27,528
[FOREIGNER] Seriously? We came all the way here,

250
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,862
now you’re telling us to leave?

251
00:16:29,279 --> 00:16:29,988
Hi there.

252
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:31,323
Excuse me?

253
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:33,783
[FOREIGNER] Out of all the Filipinas throwing themselves at me,

254
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:34,493
you’re lucky!

255
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:36,120
Hey! Stop!

256
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:36,954
What is...

257
00:16:36,995 --> 00:16:37,995
Hey!

258
00:16:37,996 --> 00:16:40,499
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

259
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:43,042
- [CAROL] Hey! Call for help! - [INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

260
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,168
[CAROL] Call the police!

261
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:46,754
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

262
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:47,756
[JAO] Kara!

263
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,133
[JAO] I’m here to listen.

264
